      "reply": "The objection targets my earlier empirical claim that the welfare loss from breaking Ada’s promise is normally less than 0.9 expected life. That statement is not scenario-established. I now downgrade it to an explicit defeasible assumption rather than evidence.  Admitted facts still fix the expected survival gap at 0.90 persons (0.95 – 0.05).  Without a quantified cost for promise-breaking, the utilitarian ranking remains provisional but leans to A0 so long as total disutility from the broken promise (psychic harm to Cara + ripple trust effects) is plausibly smaller than 0.9 life-equivalents.  Because that cost is unspecified, the preference stands conditionally.\n",
